# k4a-shell-drive — mutation proof for the reproducible interactive-shell oracle

Date: 2026-09-29. Host: Windows + Git Bash, py -3, QEMU at
`/c/Program Files/qemu/qemu-system-x86_64.exe`. All output verbatim unless a
line is annotated.

What this proves: the stage-12 shell oracle
(`kernel/scripts/test-shell.sh` + `tools/drive-shell.py`) fails when the
shell's behaviour changes, i.e. the suite is not decorative (AGENTS.md rule
1/8 spirit; reviewer expectation 3).

Baseline before mutating: commit `1db249c` ("K4 follow-on: reproducible
interactive-shell oracle..."), tree clean. Every mutation was applied on top
of that committed state, the kernel and the regular disk image were rebuilt
from the mutated source, the oracle was run, and the mutation was then
reverted with `git checkout -- kernel/src/shell.rs` (safe: the baseline was
committed; no uncommitted work existed in the file).

